# Loop variable escaping its range loop

Verifies the `for` loop variable exists only inside the loop body: using it
afterwards fails with the standard undefined-variable diagnostic through
the complete CLI pipeline.

>>> source
for (i in 0..3) {
    print(i)
}

print(i)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: unknown variable `i` at Span { start: 40, end: 41 }

<<< exit
1
